1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,480
How are we feeling about the run today, boys?

2
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:14,700
Tindalos?

3
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:15,800
Mascerville?

4
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,920
Oh, is that so?

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,540
Yeah, good job, boys.

6
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,080
It's been a few months since I arrived in Rosenberg.

7
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:29,760
I've been working with different parties as a mercenary.

8
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:34,240
Helping out on their jobs and trying to build a good reputation among the townsfolk and adventurers.

9
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:40,360
The idea is to get popular enough that word about me reaches Zenith, wherever she is.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,400
Okay, only like a hundred left to go.

11
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:44,720
Come on, Heracles!

12
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:45,640
Hulk!

13
00:00:45,640 --> 00:01:07,120
Listen up!

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,300
Step Leader has taken this S-ranked extermination job.

15
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,320
We'll clear the Snowdrake infestation out of Ilbrun Cave in no time.

16
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,900
And we'll set out immediately!

17
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:17,600
Yeah!

18
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:21,580
Hope the rest of you are ready to marvel at our greatness when we return.

19
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:38,140
Hey, Quagmire, thanks again for the other day.

20
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,240
Oh no, I should be thanking you.

21
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,620
We're leaving town today, Quagmire.

22
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:46,300
But I'll be sure to send word if I hear anything about your mother out there, alright?

23
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:47,940
Oh, thank you.

24
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:48,880
Please do.

25
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:51,740
Looks like all my hard work is starting to pay off.

26
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:56,000
Because Rudeus Greyrat now has quite the reputation in this town.

27
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:56,920
I'll take this one.

28
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:01,020
Although more people do know me by my nickname, Quagmire, than my real one.

29
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:05,780
Making a name for yourself in one town takes a few months to a year.

30
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:09,860
It feels like a hell of a long time, but right now, it's the best plan I have.

31
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,620
Isn't that right, Master Roxy?

32
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,820
I'm Rudeus Greyrat.

33
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,560
It's a pleasure to meet you.

34
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,840
You that famous Quagmire guy?

35
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:30,040
I don't know if I'm all that famous, but yes.

36
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:32,980
Well then, get to work, celebrity.

37
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:34,980
Yes, sir.

38
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:35,880
Bye.

39
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:48,440
Bye.

40
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,080
Bye.

41
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:59,080
So I'm going to do it again

42
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:03,080
I feel like I'm going to go

43
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,080
That time I'm going to go

44
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,080
Where am I going?

45
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,080
I'm going to go

46
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:11,080
I'm going to go

47
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,080
I'm not going to go

48
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,080
I'm going to go

49
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:24,080
I'm going to go

50
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:27,080
I'm going to go

51
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:32,080
You are dying

52
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:44,080
Oh, that is

53
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:52,700
Good boys, way to go.

54
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,360
On your way home?

55
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:02,540
Yes. I just finished a job, so I'll report it and head back to the inn.

56
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:10,040
Well, we were just about to pick out a new job ourselves. You want to join us?

57
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,860
Yeah, I...

58
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:17,180
I met Counter Arrow as soon as I got here, and I've worked with them a lot since.

59
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:22,360
Teaming up with one party over and over doesn't do much for my goal, but it's hard to turn them down.

60
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,460
Uh, when would you guys be heading out?

61
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:31,380
Oh my god, if you're not interested, then just say no. It's not like we're desperate.

62
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,740
Sorry about that. I'm just indecisive.

63
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:38,980
You're sorry about everything. It's kind of pathetic.

64
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,280
Sarah, that's enough.

65
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:46,120
Whatever. So, what you think? You coming?

66
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:49,940
I am. I appreciate the invite.

67
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:53,000
Well then, let's get in there and find a job, shall we?

68
00:04:53,000 --> 00:05:05,660
The Galga ruins were originally built as a fortress during the first human-demon war.

69
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:06,900
Wow.

70
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:12,760
I saw some pretty cool structures on the demon continent, but nothing quite like this.

71
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:15,620
Don't just stand there staring.

72
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,980
Oh, sorry. I'm coming.

73
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,660
Do you like architecture?

74
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:24,620
Not especially. I just haven't seen many places this impressive before, you know?

75
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,080
Here.

76
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:38,400
Hey, watch your hands, Kree.

77
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,520
I thought I was.

78
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,620
Sorry about that.

79
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:53,320
This must be the place.

80
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,340
Oh.

81
00:05:55,140 --> 00:06:00,300
All we're here to do is collect a bunch of these fancy scales, and they're just lying around everywhere.

82
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:03,100
Pretty easy for an A-class job.

83
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:09,940
This is still Snowdrake territory, so stay alert. Don't go past that statue.

84
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:11,060
Got it.

85
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:22,060
Actually, fighting the Snowdrakes would suck, but they only use this passage to get from place to place, so we can just hide if any of them show up, but...

86
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:24,300
It's a little too quiet.

87
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:34,060
You know, that buxom babe statue kind of reminds me of...

88
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,860
Talk about taking artistic license.

89
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:42,600
What was that?

90
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:45,140
I've got a bad feeling about this.

91
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,900
We're under attack!

92
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:00,420
What?

93
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,180
Why does this keep happening?

94
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:26,720
What?

95
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,240
Guys?

96
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:36,880
What?

97
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,700
What?

98
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:51,940
May the smoldering spark call for the great and searing blessing, Blamethrower!

99
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:56,980
Let's go, Patrice!

100
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,000
On it!

101
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:05,880
These things aren't after us. Just hit the ones charging towards us and knock them off course.

102
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:06,420
Gotcha!

103
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:08,040
Coming in from the left!

104
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:17,700
Don't just stand around! You're in this fight too, moron!

105
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,180
Right!

106
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,160
Haven't we had enough?

107
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,720
Alright, let's press the attack as well.

108
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,340
Thought you'd never ask!

109
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:43,560
Is it over?

110
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:56,380
Hey there! I'm Timothy of Counter Arrow. Thank you!

111
00:08:56,380 --> 00:09:03,000
You got a lot of nerve giving me that dopey smile after you try to swipe our prey.

112
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,260
Are you joking? We didn't know anyone else was working a job down here.

113
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:08,880
I announced it in front of the entire guild!

114
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,500
Well, it's news to us!

115
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:15,500
Do you know something about this, Rudeus?

116
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:22,460
Well, come to think of it, he did mention something about a job at the guild hall the other day.

117
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:27,980
I think they were going to exterminate a Snowdrake infestation in Ilbrun Cave.

118
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:33,940
In Ilbrun Cave! That's a day and a half away from here! These are the Galga ruins!

119
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:36,560
Suzanne, please, it's fine.

120
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:39,400
You okay, Timothy? How's your face feeling?

121
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:42,560
I'm fine. He was kind enough to take it easy on me.

122
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:45,020
Sarah, lower your bow, please.

123
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:49,560
I think I see what happened.

124
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:55,560
This castle was once the base for a demon king, with tunnels branching off to who knows where.

125
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,560
Maybe one of them opened up between the ruins and the cave.

126
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:01,560
So what? You're saying you came out here on a different job?

127
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:06,560
That's right. You can confirm this with the guild when you return to town, if you like.

128
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:11,560
Well, sorry for punching you out of nowhere, then.

129
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:16,560
That's all right. We both misunderstood the situation. I'm sorry we had to run into each other.

130
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:20,560
Well, I don't care how many you killed. These drakes were still our prey.

131
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:23,560
We'll let you claim one quarts, but that's it. You understand me?

132
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,560
Yes, of course.

133
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:34,560
Okay, then. Let's gather up our scales and head on back to town. We can celebrate together once we get there.

134
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:38,560
You got it, boss. I need a drink after this.

135
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:42,560
Hey, Rudeus. You should come to the after party for once.

136
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,560
Huh?

137
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,560
Well then.

138
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,560
Cheers!

139
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,560
Cheers!

140
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:58,560
Feels good to have made it out of that mess without losing anyone, though it was pretty close for a minute there.

141
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:01,560
Yeah, you got really lucky, Rudeus.

142
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:04,560
Was that luck? Felt more like you guys rescued me.

143
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:09,560
Yeah, and you're lucky that we did. Most parties would have left you to die out there.

144
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,560
Well, I'm grateful.

145
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:13,560
Don't thank me.

146
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:18,560
You should be thanking Timothy and Suzanne. They deserve all the credit.

147
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:24,560
Oh, you say that now, but you're the one who rushed back in before any of us.

148
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,560
You insisted that we could save him.

149
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,560
Shut up, Suzanne!

150
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:33,560
You helped us out last time with the Grizzlies, so I wanted to return the favor.

151
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:36,560
I don't like being in anyone's debt, and that's all there is to it.

152
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,560
In any case, we made it back in one piece.

153
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,560
And got plenty of cash.

154
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,560
That's my kind of job.

155
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:48,560
Although, shame we had to run into that jerk.

156
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,560
Would have been even better if we hadn't.

157
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:56,560
Yeah, being the toughest party in the guild made them pretty insufferable.

158
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:59,560
I wish they'd stick to their damn labyrinths.

159
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:02,560
And that jackass calls himself a party leader.

160
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:06,560
I can't help but wonder if Paul was like that when he was younger.

161
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:21,560
What do you want?

162
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:26,560
I was all worked up back in the cave, so I thought I'd come set things straight with you people.

163
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:30,560
I didn't know what was going on, and I kinda screwed up.

164
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,560
So guess what I'm trying to say?

165
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:35,560
That was my bad or whatever.

166
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:40,560
With that said, her face just pisses me off, man.

167
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:44,560
Always grinning like an idiot, and then you just let a guy punch you like that?

168
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,560
Didn't even argue or nothing.

169
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:49,560
You're just all smiles and bruises, and I hate that shit.

170
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,560
Sometimes a man's gotta fight, you feel me?

171
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,560
Well, yes, perhaps you're right.

172
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,560
Suzanne often tells me I'm too passive.

173
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:58,560
I'll remember that.

174
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:05,560
Good, yeah, you remember that.

175
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:08,560
Now, Quagmire.

176
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,560
Yes?

177
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:14,560
Timmy hears one thing, but I can't stand your ass, kid.

178
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:18,560
You got this weird people-pleasing attitude, but no one's buying it.

179
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:21,560
Yeah, and that creepy grin of yours makes me sick.

180
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,560
Maybe you think that's a smile, but it ain't.

181
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,560
Try a little harder.

182
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,560
We can see the contempt in your eyes.

183
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:29,560
Who do you think you are, huh?

184
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,560
Come on, let go of me.

185
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,560
Give it a rest, all right?

186
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,560
Look at him!

187
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,560
This dumb-faced, pouty-crymouth.

188
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,560
You're the saddest boy in the world.

189
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,560
I don't know what happened to you, Quagmire, but you're depressing.

190
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:43,560
So you can either learn to man up and face your stupid problems,

191
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,560
or get the hell out of my guild!

192
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:50,560
I didn't realize I bothered you so much.

193
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,560
I'll do my best to stay out of your sight from now on.

194
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,560
Oh, bullshit!

195
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,560
What is that supposed to mean?

196
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,560
Are you trying to piss me off?!

197
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:02,560
Is it fun for you acting like a martyr all the time,

198
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,560
or acting like you're too good for money?

199
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:07,560
We all need cash to survive, you brat!

200
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:10,560
That's enough, soul. Go sleep this off.

201
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,560
Shut up!

202
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:12,560
Let me go, Conrad.

203
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,560
Hey, listen, Quagmire.

204
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,560
If you hate your life so much, drop dead!

205
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:19,560
At least then I won't have to see your stupid face again

206
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,560
until I'm sick of your shit!

207
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:27,560
Ugh, that guy is the worst.

208
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:50,560
Oh, waiting for cheap jobs again?

209
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,560
I have my reasons for doing this.

210
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,560
Well, I bet your reasons suck.

211
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:57,560
You half-ass everything you ever do, don't you?

212
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,560
I have my own idea.

213
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,560
Hello.

214
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,560
Oh, it's Rudeus.

215
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,560
Is something wrong?

216
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,560
It's Mimir and Sarah.

217
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:23,560
Are they okay?

218
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,560
They're both dead.

219
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,560
Oh.

220
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,560
I...

221
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:34,560
No. Mimir is dead, but Sarah just got separated.

222
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:36,560
If we leave now, we may still be able to find her.

223
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:41,560
If we try to go back out right now in this blizzard, we'll die long before we ever find her.

224
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:46,560
We shouldn't have left. I shouldn't have made the call.

225
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:51,560
We all agreed to run. We're equally responsible, okay?

226
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:54,560
Um, where did you lose her?

227
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:57,560
In Trier Forest, to the west.

228
00:15:57,560 --> 00:16:02,560
The blizzard blinded us, and then a herd of snow buffalo attacked.

229
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:07,560
I see. That must have been awful. But I should be going.

230
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:31,560
Well, I bet your reasons suck. You half-ass everything you ever do, don't you?

231
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:39,600
Well, I bet your reasons suck.

232
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,480
You half-ass everything you ever do, don't you?

233
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,800
Maybe he was right. What the hell am I doing out here alone?

234
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,460
Stroking my own ego?

235
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:54,240
Of course I want to find Sarah, but I don't think I even care if she's alive or dead.

236
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:57,580
Maybe I just want to take action and have something to show for it.

237
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:00,460
Get a result, any result.

238
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:05,680
Or maybe I wanted to actively make the choice not to abandon someone.

239
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,220
The way Eris abandoned me.

240
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,220
That could be all there is to it.

241
00:17:15,420 --> 00:17:18,400
But what if I do find her?

242
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:23,260
I don't know. Maybe I shouldn't get my hopes up.

243
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:27,740
I'm not going to accomplish anything here.

244
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:29,340
How could I?

245
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:36,740
Is that Mimir?

246
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:52,700
Where is Sarah?

247
00:17:52,700 --> 00:18:19,720
It's not like Sarah and I were close or anything, but she hadn't been nearly as prickly lately.

248
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:38,700
I bet we could have been friends eventually.

249
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:45,700
Sarah!

250
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,700
Sarah!

251
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:47,700
Sarah!

252
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:54,700
Sarah!

253
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:55,700
Sarah!

254
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,700
Who's there?

255
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:00,700
It's Rudeus.

256
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,700
Rudeus?

257
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:17,700
I'm here to save you.

258
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:42,700
I'm here to save you.

259
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,700
